---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const inquiry = 'mailto:hello@kenashe.ai?subject=Sponsored%20test%20or%20build';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Work with me"
  description="Sponsor an honest, hands-on test or AI build with Ken Ashe. Real tasks, documented results, clear sponsorship disclosure, and independent conclusions."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Work with me', path: '/work/' }]}
>
  <article class="work-page">
    <header>
      <p class="mark">// work with me</p>
      <h1>Sponsor an honest test or build.</h1>
      <p class="lede">A real tool. A real task. An honest account of what happened.</p>
      <p>I build agents, automations, and AI-assisted websites. If your product fits that work,
        we can agree on a practical experiment and document the results, including the limits.</p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="pilot">
      <h2 id="pilot">Start with one focused project</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>One agreed task, workflow, or build that puts the product to use.</li>
        <li>A hands-on test and one original article on this site, with evidence of what worked and what did not.</li>
        <li>One factual-review round before publication. Conclusions stay independent.</li>
        <li>Clear sponsorship disclosure near the beginning of the article.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Video, social posts, and additional deliverables can be scoped separately. This is not
        a placement in the automated Digest; it is a separately agreed, hands-on project.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="boundaries">
      <h2 id="boundaries">What a sponsorship does not buy</h2>
      <p>Payment covers the agreed work, not a positive review. I do not guarantee views,
        sales, search rankings, or links that pass ranking credit. Paid links are marked as sponsored.</p>
      <p>Advertising use, republication, exclusivity, and ownership transfers are not included
        unless we agree on them in writing. Final deliverables, timing, payment terms, and any
        product access or testing costs are agreed before work starts.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="inquiry" aria-labelledby="brief">
      <h2 id="brief">Send me the brief</h2>
      <p>Tell me what the product does, who it serves, the task you want tested, your budget
        range, timing, and where you want to use the finished work. I will scope the project
        and quote it before we commit.</p>
      <a class="email" href={inquiry}>Discuss a sponsored test →</a>
      <p class="small">Prefer a plain email? <a href="mailto:hello@kenashe.ai">hello@kenashe.ai</a></p>
    </section>

    <p class="elsewhere">For AI systems and automation projects, email me with the problem you want solved.
      Domain acquisition, brokerage, and SEO services are available through
      <a href="https://luckydomains.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lucky Domains</a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .work-page { max-width: var(--content-width); margin: 0 auto; padding: 4rem 1.5rem 0; font-family: var(--font-sans); color: var(--fg); line-height: 1.7; }
  .mark { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .8125rem; color: var(--accent); letter-spacing: .1em; }
  h1 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem); line-height: 1.06; letter-spacing: -.035em; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
  .lede { font-size: 1.25rem; }
  section { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-top: 1.5rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.25; }
  p, li { max-width: var(--reading-width); }
  li { margin: .6rem 0; }
  a { color: var(--accent); text-underline-offset: .2em; }
  .inquiry { background: var(--surface); padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; }
  .inquiry h2 { margin-top: 0; }
  .email { display: inline-block; padding: .75rem 1rem; background: var(--accent); color: var(--bg); border-radius: 5px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 700; }
  .small, .elsewhere { font-size: .9375rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .elsewhere { margin-top: 2rem; }
</style>
